;;; A qualified import brings the module's query, lattice and configuration
;;; — M1f **W90**, register row `W90/import-directives-as`
;;; (`corpus/wrong_answers.toml`), filed by S1f.6.25 (T1f.6.25.2, 2026-11-13)
;;; from E-8 of P1f.6's `findings.md`.
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `import-directives-module.ein`, beside this file, declares `is-a`, states
;;; `(is-a Tea Drink)`, and then says what a *program* says: `(solve
;;; :hypothesis-relations ())`, a `(config …)` flag and a `(query …)`. This
;;; program imports it `:as m`, declares one relation of its own, `chosen`,
;;; closes the imported one, and states no lattice, no flag and no query.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; The program states no `(solve …)`, so its hypotheses are the facts of its
;;; open declared relation over its names: `(chosen Drink)` and `(chosen
;;; Tea)`. Nothing restricts them, so R is the whole cube, four states. It
;;; asks no query, so the read-out answers none.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ───────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `5e5685b7`, release: the module's `(solve :hypothesis-relations ())`
;;; came with the import, so there was no candidate and R was {∅}, one state;
;;; the read-out answered the module's query, renamed, `(m.is-a ?x Drink)`,
;;; *Tea is a drink*; and `--dump-config` showed the module's flag. A flat
;;; import of the same module brought none of the three.

(import import-directives-module :as m)

(relation chosen Thing :why "{?1} is chosen")
(__closed__ m.is-a)
